# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. results/calibration slim-bundle rules. Bundles are committed slim: only the
#    text files (meta/run_config/metrics/legitimacy_diagnostics/attestation/
#    SUMMARY) + the dashboard payload. The per-hour dispatch dir, system/storage/
#    btm/scarcity/availability/posture/flows parquets, floors, solve logs and the
#    captured model_changes.diff are large regenerable intermediates. Rules cover
#    both the flat (results/calibration/<name>/) and ISO-scoped
#    (results/calibration/<ISO>/<name>/) bundle layouts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# caiso-288 (2026-09-20) per-year SHARD LEGS. Rule 32 [R-SHARD] (d): per-year
# shard bundle dirs are KEPT OUT OF `main` — the parent fetches them, composes,
# and commits only the composite (here `caiso288_gasfix_span`, the registered
# keeper). An unregistered per-year dir left committed is the exact Class-E
# parity RED rule 29 [R-SCREEN] (c) forbids. Ignored rather than deleted, per
# rule 31 [R-RETAIN]: ".gitignore is what discharges the delete-before-merge
# duty, not `rm`". Nothing is lost — each leg's FULL bundle (incl.
# dispatch/<year>_P1.parquet) is pushed on its own shard branch under rule 34
# [R-SHARD-PROMOTABLE] (a), recoverable at ZERO LP by immutable SHA:
#   git checkout 8c19a3aeddad -- results/calibration/caiso288_gasfix_2023
#   git checkout 9bf1e0bad0ec -- results/calibration/caiso288_gasfix_2024
#   git checkout 887bb239e27e -- results/calibration/caiso288_gasfix_2025
# (2022 leg: aac324c4b211dd33e028e3a0bd1ba50e2e44d7f7 — its bundle IS registered,
#  as the stamped rung 2026-09-20-caiso-288-citygate-2022, so it is not ignored.)
# Full recovery table: docs/RESULT-caiso288-the-prints-were-published-2026-09-20.md §7.
results/calibration/caiso288_gasfix_2023/
results/calibration/caiso288_gasfix_2024/
results/calibration/caiso288_gasfix_2025/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hydro-1 (2026-09-22) per-year ARM LEGS, three arms x their keeper year sets.
# Same rule 32 [R-SHARD] (d) posture as the caiso-288 block above: per-year arm
# bundles are KEPT OUT OF `main`, and ignored rather than deleted per rule 31
# [R-RETAIN] — ".gitignore is what discharges the delete-before-merge duty, not
# `rm`". NONE of these is a registered run: arm A/B are promotion CANDIDATES
# whose lanes (hydro-2 / hydro-3) must first close their outstanding year, and
# arm C is REFUTED, so committing any of them would be the Class-E parity RED
# rule 29 [R-SCREEN] (c) forbids.
#
# Every number these bundles support is in docs/RESULT-hydro-1-2026-09-22.md —
# that doc is the record, exactly as rule 31 intends. The SHAs below are
# PROVENANCE (which commit produced which leg), NOT a durability claim: a shard
# branch is transport and is cut when the lane's PR merges (rule 33
# [R-SHARD-ARCHIVE] (d)/(f)). Cost any leg not landed on `main` as a RE-SOLVE —
# NYISO is ~3.5 min of LP per year, PJM longer.
#
#   arm A2 hydro_ror_split, PJM vs pjm_h15_coalwindow_span   (cell O, candidate)
#     git checkout c6549ea720c4 -- results/calibration/hydro1_pjm_ror2_2024
#     git checkout 404b9276c670 -- results/calibration/hydro1_pjm_ror2_2025
#   arm B  hydro_ror_split, NYISO vs nyiso247_fuelinv_span   (cell O, candidate)
#     git checkout d09eb5868fce -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2022
#     git checkout 7dba706d6253 -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2023
#     git checkout 1caea62bb36c -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2024
#     git checkout 136bea23f813 -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2025
#   arm C  hydro_pondage_bound, NYISO                        (cell R, REFUTED)
#     git checkout 238194935888 -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2022
#     git checkout ee044e642ff9 -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2023
#     git checkout 0b95a6d5fdf2 -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2024
#     git checkout 2537e6bac109 -- results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2025
#   (hydro1_pjm_ror_2025 @ 693f5e9bc309 is the SUPERSEDED h13-control leg,
#    kept only because rule 31 forbids deleting it before the owner rules.)
results/calibration/hydro1_pjm_ror2_2024/
results/calibration/hydro1_pjm_ror2_2025/
results/calibration/hydro1_pjm_ror_2025/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2022/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2023/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2024/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_ror_2025/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2022/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2023/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2024/
results/calibration/hydro1_nyiso_pond_2025/

results/calibration/*/model_changes.diff
results/calibration/*/dispatch/
results/calibration/*/*.parquet
results/calibration/*/floors/
# Per-unit / per-link hourly sidecars — excluded BY DEFAULT; bundles normally
# commit only hourly/{class_hourly,storage,system,reserve_family} (rule 15).
#
# The two grounds this exclusion used to state ("~58 MB/bundle", "regenerable by
# a replay") were both MEASURED FALSE at nyiso-116 (2026-08-03) and are corrected
# here rather than left to mislead:
#   * SIZE — NYISO measures 920 KB/yr (unit) + 170 KB/yr (network) = 3.2 MB for a
#     whole 3-year bundle. The ~58 MB figure predates the DELTA_BINARY_PACKED
#     ``hour`` encoding (see _write_hourly_sidecar's docstring: CAISO's unit frame
#     went 12.60 MB -> 1.74 MB from that change alone).
#   * REPLAY — nyiso-114 §2 measured that a keeper arming a P0-run-pattern bridge
#     CANNOT be re-solved into byte-identity once main has moved (caiso-155 vertex
#     dependence), so for such a keeper this layer is PERMANENTLY unrecoverable.
#
# So the default stays (these are still the bundle's largest frames and most
# bundles are never interrogated at unit grain), but a lane that WILL interrogate
# a bundle commits its layer deliberately with ``git add -f`` — see the
# unit_network_layer_sidecar matrix row. Opt-in per bundle, not a policy flip.
results/calibration/*/hourly/unit_hourly_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/hourly/network_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/hourly/unit_hourly_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/hourly/network_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/solve.log
results/calibration/*-capdel-probe.log
# miso-188: replay launch logs (transient stdout capture of in-session
# replay_keeper invocations; the solve itself writes the ignored solve.log)
results/calibration/*.launch.log
results/calibration/*/_shared/
results/calibration/_shared/
# Same derived shared-input cache when a run uses an --out-dir OUTSIDE
# results/calibration/ (e.g. --out-dir results/<probe>): the sibling
# _shared/ then lands at results/_shared/, which the two rules above miss.
results/_shared/
results/calibration/logs/
# ISO-scoped (two-level) bundle internals — the single-* rules above miss them.
results/calibration/*/*/model_changes.diff
results/calibration/*/*/dispatch/
results/calibration/*/*/floors/
results/calibration/*/*/system.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/storage.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/btm.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/availability_rcpf*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/scarcity*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/posture.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/flows.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/solve.log
results/calibration/*/*/_shared/

# Probe-local CLEAN trees. The offer-surface probes curate into their own clean
# root under results/calibration/ (the `--clean-root` default of
# _caiso152_rle_parse_bias.py and _caiso153_offer_classifier_reid.py), which is
# DERIVED, disposable data in the sense of the data/clean/ contract — ~234 MB
# for the CAISO 2023-25 dam-public-bids span, regenerable by re-running
# `curate`. It is never an input to a committed result and must never enter a
# pack (the remote rejects large packs with HTTP 413).
results/calibration/clean_*/
results/calibration/*/clean_*/

# Session-local CLEAN staging. A partition-restoration A/B (caiso-157) has to
# move curated partitions in and out of data/clean around each arm so each arm
# solves the input state it declares; the holding area is the same DERIVED,
# disposable data as data/clean itself and is regenerable by re-running the
# curate scripts. Never an input to a committed result.
.clean_stash/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. results/calibration & results/hindcast scratch families — recurring
#    throwaway-probe naming (rule 14/16: never registered keepers; regenerable
#    from run_config.json). One-off per-session dir names are NOT enumerated;
#    their heavy contents are already ignored by §8.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/calibration/*probe*/
# miso-fuelvintage-1 (2026-09-09) working bundles: the rule-29 [R-SCREEN] screen
# arm (2024) and the full-span promotion candidate for
# gas_electric_power_monthly_level. Ignored so they can never reach `main`, which
# is the ONLY thing rule 29(c) DELETE-BEFORE-MERGE requires; rule 31 [R-RETAIN]
# names gitignoring — never `rm` — as what discharges it, so these stay on local
# disk until the OWNER has ruled on promotion. The promoted bundle's slim set
# overrides this rule via `git add -f`.
results/screen/miso_ep_level_*/
results/calibration/miso_fuelvintage_*/
# miso-248 SPP-ladder clock re-derive: the rule-29 screen arm + its EARNED
# control (G-DRIFT found one LIVE hunk, so form 4 is falsified) and, if the
# screen clears, the full-span bundle. Rule 29(c) DELETE-BEFORE-MERGE is
# discharged by keeping them out of `main`, which this rule does; rule 31
# [R-RETAIN] forbids removing them from disk before the owner rules on
# promotion. A promoted bundle's slim set overrides this rule via `git add -f`.
results/calibration/miso248_*/
