# NEISO-RC-R R4 tracked-set change (2026-08-31; FINDING-capx-neiso-rc-phase0
# §6 R4): a CROSSOVER bundle's per-year evolution ledgers ARE the committed
# record — the capxd14-era three-file bundles left every mechanism claim
# about them unverifiable (lag-censored retirement decisions unobservable;
# the scorer's retirement_decisions_in_window block needs pipeline_events).
# KB-scale JSON, same class as the committed S-4b T1-F ledgers.
!results/hindcast/*crossover*/*/*/evolution_*.json
# capx-D27 tracked-set addition (2026-09-01; FINDING-capx-d17-miso-exit-channel
# §6 R1, which asked the re-measure to COMMIT "the hindcast per-fuel depths, bar
# decompositions and event rows this lane had to bound around"). This ONE T1-H
# bundle's per-year ledgers are the sole evidence for its central mechanism
# claim — that `_floor_retention_merit`'s ascending cost-per-firm-MW ordering,
# not admission depth, is what makes the released exit set 100 % coal — so
# without them a future lane must re-solve (~35 min) to check it. Deliberately
# scoped to this bundle, NOT to the T1-H class: the slim-set convention above is
# unchanged for every other hindcast run. 3.0 MB of JSON across 5 files.
!results/hindcast/miso-2021-2025-realized-t1h-d27/*/*/evolution_*.json
# capx D31 (2026-09-02): same one-bundle-scoped carve-out as the d27 rule above
