# NOTE (SPP-48, corrected 2026-09-19): the arm bundle is deliberately NOT
# ignored at DIRECTORY grain. Git will not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a shard's `!results/calibration/spp48_arm_span/**` negation can never
# re-include anything inside one — `git add` then fails with "paths are ignored
# by one of your .gitignore files", and the only way through is `git add -f`,
# which the auto-mode classifier REFUSES as [Modify Shared Resources]. That is
# the miso-255 stranding, one layer over. Reproduced in a scratch repo both
# ways before this line was removed: with the directory ignored, 0 of 6 bundle
# files stage; without it, 6 of 6 do, because the generic
# `results/calibration/*/dispatch/`-class rules leave the PARENT visible and a
# `/**` negation can then override them. The arm bundle is a single registrable
# span (rule 34 [R-SHARD-PROMOTABLE] (a) requires the shard to PUSH it), so the
# parent simply does not commit it to main rather than ignoring it.
