#
# DELETION WAS ATTEMPTED AND REFUSED. `git push origin --delete` returns HTTP 403
# for all nine claude/nwpp-42-* refs: this session's credential can CREATE and
# UPDATE refs but not DELETE them, and the GitHub MCP server exposes create_branch
# with no counterpart. That is the exact failure rule 33 [R-SHARD-ARCHIVE] (f)(5)
# documents, and (f)(5) says to SAY SO and leave the branch rather than report a
# cleanup that did not happen. The refs are therefore still listed until the owner
# removes them; they are RETIRED, meaning nothing may depend on them.
#
# THE `git checkout <sha> -- <path>` LINES ABOVE ARE A PROVENANCE RECORD, NOT A
# RECOVERY ROUTE (rule 33(f)(4)). Treat recovery as RE-SOLVE ONLY, ~45-90 min of LP
# per leg, whether or not a ref happens to still resolve today.
#
# WHY RETIRING THEM COSTS NOTHING MAIN DOES NOT ALREADY CARRY:
#   * Rule 31 [R-RETAIN] trigger (i) is satisfied -- the owner RULED on promotion, so
#     a spent bundle may be removed and "git history plus the RESULT doc remain the
#     record". The RESULT doc is docs/handoffs/FINDING-nwpp-42-2026-09-20.md and it
#     carries every number this lane will ever cite from any of the six legs.
#   * The KEEPER is registered and on main: results/calibration/nwpp42_coalhr_span
#     (slim hourly/ shape, rule 15 [R-DASHBOARD]) plus its registry sidecar and its
#     run payload under frontend/data/backcast/runs/. The per-plant D-1/D-2/D-4
#     diagnostics fall back to the REGISTERED PAYLOAD when dispatch/<year>_P1.parquet
#     is absent, and that payload is committed -- so nothing on the dashboard or in
#     the scorer depends on these refs.
#   * The CONTROL legs were never eligible for main: rule 29 [R-SCREEN] (c) forbids a
#     control bundle reaching main and rule 15's keeper-only retention forbids a
#     second registered NWPP run. The FINDING is where their numbers live, by design.
#   * The three arm legs' dispatch/ layer would have added ~45 MB to a repo whose tip
#     is already 4.13 GiB packed and which has needed two history rewrites.
#     .gitignore line ~651 ignores results/calibration/*/dispatch/ repo-wide for that
#     reason.
#
# THE LESSON, recorded because it bit twice in one session: an unmerged shard branch
# is NOT durable here. The environment deleted claude/nwpp-42-{arm-2023,arm-2024,
# mer-2025} when the PARENT's PR merged -- not only branches that were themselves
# merged -- and then deleted the lane branch on its own merge. A lane that needs
# bytes to survive must land them on MAIN, inside the registered keeper bundle,
# before its own PR merges. It must NOT park them on a side ref: side refs are both
# undurable AND un-deletable from a session, which is the worst of both.
results/calibration/nwpp42_coalhr_2023/
results/calibration/nwpp42_coalhr_2024/
results/calibration/nwpp42_coalhr_2025/
results/calibration/nwpp42_mer_2023/
results/calibration/nwpp42_mer_2024/
results/calibration/nwpp42_mer_2025/
#
# nwpp42_mer_span is the composed CONTROL — NWPP-41's own recipe re-solved under
# rule-36 year isolation. Rule 29 [R-SCREEN] (c): a control bundle is never
# registered and never reaches main, so it is ignored here rather than deleted
# (rule 31 [R-RETAIN]; `rm` is never required). Every number this lane cites
# from it is in docs/handoffs/FINDING-nwpp-42-2026-09-20.md, and it recomposes
# for free from the three mer legs above with
# scripts/probes/_nwpp42_compose_span.py. The ARM composite
# results/calibration/nwpp42_coalhr_span/ is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the
# registered run and its slim keeper file set is committed.
results/calibration/nwpp42_mer_span/
# caiso-287: per-year instrumented + MER control shard bundles. Pushed by each
# shard to its OWN branch (rule 34 [R-SHARD-PROMOTABLE] (a)) and kept out of
# main from the parent's tree (rule 32(d)); never `rm` (rule 31 [R-RETAIN]).
#
# WHAT IS ALREADY ON MAIN AND NEEDS NO RECOVERY: the promoted keeper
# caiso287_mer_span and its 2022 touchpoint caiso287_instr_2022 are COMMITTED
# (registered 2026-09-19), INCLUDING their hourly/p0_dispatch_<year>.parquet
# and hourly/p0_prices_<year>.parquet. So the arrays the screen split was
# measured from are on main; only the per-year dispatch/ and floors/ are not
# (the standard slim-bundle rule above).
#
# RECOVERY, BY FULL IMMUTABLE SHA, NEVER BRANCH NAME (rule 33(d)). Branch
# deletion is REFUSED for this session's credential (HTTP 403, rule 33(f)(5)),
# so these branches are left for the environment's own auto-disposal; while the
# branch survives the sha is fetchable, and once it is gone the sha becomes
# unreachable and eventually GC'd.
#   git checkout bb3034214d1d3da70d0db8d8435540f82387222d -- results/calibration/caiso287_instr_2022
#   git checkout 8ce50d15cbd3ffd789978ec8c2389666c8a62439 -- results/calibration/caiso287_instr_2023
#   git checkout b0e56a2ea90541c0ef3b8c840aa16c65cdff85d6 -- results/calibration/caiso287_instr_2025
#   git checkout ba322129dfdf46669a9d7f776f3b38027a8ec528 -- results/calibration/caiso_mer_2022_2026-09-19
#   git checkout cf45350227029d923f94cc1f8cea8c18bb034aa4 -- results/calibration/caiso_mer_2023
#   git checkout 2f818efb8e5a21490114e03689896441348959df -- results/calibration/caiso_mer_2024
#
# DEAD PIN, RECORDED HONESTLY (rule 33(f)(4)): the 2024 instrumented bundle came
# from claude/caiso-287-probe-2024 at d8e7b39c1e4d17e3c5c53780987b24ac80e8ee2d,
# and THAT BRANCH WAS AUTO-DELETED WITHOUT MERGING. The sha resolves only in a
# clone that already fetched it; from a fresh clone it does not. Recovery there
# is a RE-SOLVE (~23 min, 8.28 GiB peak on CAISO 2024), not a checkout -- but
# its P0 arrays are on main inside caiso287_mer_span, and every number this lane
# cites from it is in results/calibration/_caiso287_*_2024.json.
results/calibration/caiso287_instr_*/
results/calibration/caiso_mer_*/

# neiso-112 (2026-09-19): the six YEAR-ISOLATED MER bundles (rule 36
# [R-YEAR-ISOLATION]). Kept OUT OF `main` per rule 32 [R-SHARD] (d) — the parent
# never commits per-year dirs — and kept ON DISK per rule 31 [R-RETAIN], which
# forbids deleting a result before the owner has ruled on promotion. Each was
# pushed in full (17 files, incl. dispatch/<y>_P1.parquet) to its own shard
# branch under rule 34 [R-SHARD-PROMOTABLE] (a), so a promotion costs ZERO
# re-solves. Recover any of them by IMMUTABLE SHA (rule 33 [R-SHARD-ARCHIVE] (d)
# — never by branch name; the branches are deliberately NOT deleted while the
# promotion is open, per rule 33 (f)(3)):
#   git checkout c36b794b5b6363db3255edcca929ccf7d74768f4 -- results/calibration/neiso112_mer_2020
#   git checkout 5b4833a80833ac65ba2bd7554819a027b6d64e0b -- results/calibration/neiso112_mer_2021
#   git checkout a5f3a9a430249708448425d9459a6ec1f7b6cdb5 -- results/calibration/neiso112_mer_2022
#   git checkout 49c7022f48fac32952d4290980826fb8e8f85175 -- results/calibration/neiso112_mer_2023
#   git checkout b67072908d9deaec03e8ff14d120eaada40fc1e6 -- results/calibration/neiso112_mer_2024
#   git checkout 165f1db0b25939e0d60215c15611edbd9a1464c2 -- results/calibration/neiso112_mer_2025
# NOTE (rule 31, pjm-h8 correction): check_registry_payload_parity.py walks the
# FILESYSTEM, so these dirs turn that gate RED in a working tree that holds them
# while CI (which sees only committed files) stays green. That RED is expected
# here and is NEVER fixed by deleting a bundle this rule protects.
# NOTE the pattern is year-scoped on purpose: `neiso112_mer_*` would also swallow
# the COMPOSED span bundle `neiso112_mer_span`, which is the registered keeper and
# MUST commit its slim set (rule 15 [R-DASHBOARD]).
results/calibration/neiso112_mer_20[0-9][0-9]/

