# miso-263 (2026-09-19): the six PER-YEAR coal-ceiling repair bundles.
#
# Rule 32 [R-SHARD] (d) keeps per-year shard dirs OUT of `main` — the COMPOSED
# span is what gets registered — and rule 31 [R-RETAIN] says the way to
# discharge that is `.gitignore`, never `rm`. Nothing here is deleted: every
# bundle is on its own shard branch at a full immutable SHA, and a promotion
# from this state costs ZERO re-solves.
#
#   git checkout 34543fa20aeac6b4d7e7f6ef661a81c32401d437 -- results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_2020
#   git checkout ba84be60f3ccdbe0c123c09bbef052b3a38e254a -- results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_2021
#   git checkout cfacc9044cfd3dc18046735e00ac6c26e8565ed7 -- results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_2022
#   git checkout c64a50c9f715a22cc9b3d296b1dbde016f3ab052 -- results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_2025   [SUPERSEDED]
#   git checkout 4b30d39c7d446c34539db1fcfa3f041b61355b7b -- results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_2024   [SUPERSEDED]
#
# The two marked SUPERSEDED solved 2024/2025 on the VALIDATION leg's reserve
# configuration: replay_keeper.py takes its recipe from the span-wide meta.json,
# which for this composite carries the 2020 leg's values, and MISO's keeper is
# partitioned at 2023 (miso_measured_reserve_requirements / miso_reserve_online_gated
# are False for 2020-2022 and True for 2023-2025). They are kept, not deleted
# (rule 31 [R-RETAIN]); they are simply not composable. 2020/2021/2022 are
# UNAFFECTED — their own per-year flags match the composite base. See
# docs/ADDENDUM-miso263-replay-keeper-has-no-per-year-dimension-2026-09-19.md.
# Corrected 2023/2024/2025 shards push to claude/miso263-coalcap-<year>b:
#
#   git checkout d2bf6e4bec19a7b8966f310a9dd5a4d332b1ff06 -- results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_2023
#   (2024b / 2025b SHAs appended when they land)
#
# The two SUPERSEDED branches were NOT deleted, and that is not an oversight:
# `git push origin --delete` returns HTTP 403 here (this session's credential
# can create and update refs but not delete them), and the GitHub MCP server
# exposes create_branch with no counterpart. Rule 33 [R-SHARD-ARCHIVE] (f)(5):
# say so and leave the branch rather than report a cleanup that did not happen.
# The symptom is misleading — plain `git push` prints `send-pack: unexpected
# disconnect` then `Everything up-to-date`, which reads like the HTTP/2 flake;
# on HTTP/1.1 the 403 is visible. Do not retry it. A merged shard branch is
# auto-deleted by the environment, which is the normal disposal route.
# Because the branches persist, the checkout commands above STILL RESOLVE
# (rule 33 (f)(4) — nothing is re-pinned to a dead sha).
#
# The pattern is YEAR-SCOPED on purpose: `miso263_coalcap_*` would also swallow
# the composed `miso263_coalcap_span`, which is the registrable run and MUST
# commit its slim set (rule 15 [R-DASHBOARD]).
results/calibration/miso263_coalcap_20[0-9][0-9]/

# pjm-h11 (2026-09-19): the C-1 per-year shard bundles (2 arms x 6 years). Rule
# 32 [R-SHARD] (d) / 29 [R-SCREEN] (c): a per-year shard dir is kept OUT of main
# — only a composed, registered run goes there — and rule 31 [R-RETAIN] says
# .gitignore is what discharges that, never `rm`. These are RESULTS: the owner
# has not yet ruled on promotion, so nothing here is deleted.
# Bytes live on immutable shard commits (rule 33 [R-SHARD-ARCHIVE] (d) — a FULL
# sha, never a branch name, because shard branches are deleted or force-moved):
#   git checkout f3bf920ddfa9d4bd86be1c71b2984647b89d0681 -- results/calibration/pjm_h11_ctl_2020
#   git checkout e24901cb6dacd2ec6daaeafe86e7a6e4b0252c55 -- results/calibration/pjm_h11_ctl_2021
#   git checkout 3510c19c16d9913d3920ea29c3c6c0f4c7736d16 -- results/calibration/pjm_h11_ctl_2023
# The remaining nine land on claude/pjm-h11-{ctl,arm}-<year>-r2; their recovery
# shas are recorded in docs/RESULT-pjm-h11-*.md as each one reports.
#
# NOTE for any later r3 shard: this is a DIRECTORY-grain ignore, and git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a shard's `!<bundle>/**` negation cannot
# re-include anything under it (the SPP-48 stranding, .gitignore ~line 2416).
# The live shards are unaffected — they are pinned to 0fae26c3 / 3b719484, which
# predate this block. A future r3 must likewise pin to a sha before it, or use a
# bundle name outside this glob.
#
# NARROWED 2026-09-20 at the promotion, and narrowed rather than negated for the
# reason the NOTE above gives: `results/calibration/pjm_h11_*/` also swallowed the
# two COMPOSED spans, which rule 15 [R-DASHBOARD] requires to reach main, and a
# `!<dir>/**` negation under a directory-grain exclude cannot pull them back. So
# the exclude now names the per-year LEGS only. The composed dirs
# pjm_h11_{keeper,touchpoint}_span fall outside it and commit their slim set, the
# same set every PJM keeper commits (the dispatch/, floors/, root *.parquet,
# unit_hourly and network rules above still match inside them).
results/calibration/pjm_h11_arm_*/
results/calibration/pjm_h11_ctl_*/
# caiso-287: the 2022 leg became the REGISTERED touchpoint at the 2026-09-19 MER
# promotion, so it must reach main (rule 15 [R-DASHBOARD]) — un-ignore the dir
# only. The slim-bundle rules above (dispatch/, floors/, root *.parquet,
# unit_hourly, network) still match the files inside and still apply, so this
# commits the slim set every keeper commits, not the 50 MB working bundle.
!results/calibration/caiso287_instr_2022/

# caiso-292 (2026-09-20): THAT NEGATION IS NOW STALE, so the exclusion is
# restored below it (last matching rule wins). It was written because the 2022
# leg was the REGISTERED touchpoint of the 2026-09-19 MER promotion and so had
# to reach `main` under rule 15 [R-DASHBOARD]. That run was PRUNED at the
# xiso-8 promotion: CAISO carries exactly one registered run
# (2026-09-20-caiso-290-leftedge), `git ls-tree -r origin/main` returns ZERO
# files under this path, and nothing in frontend/data/backcast/,
# results/regression-goldens/ or check_registry_payload_parity
# .KEEP_REQUIRED_UNMAPPED_BUNDLES names it. So the negation no longer lets a
# registered bundle through -- it only leaves a 59 MB RECOVERY CHECKOUT exposed
# to `git add`, which would put a superseded run back on `main` against rule
# 15's keeper-only retention.
#
# caiso-292 recovered this bundle read-only to validate its screen-split
# harness (G-V1: this lane's probe == caiso-287's own probe at the same HEAD,
# 0.000e+00 MW). Rule 31 [R-RETAIN] says `.gitignore` -- never `rm` -- is what
# keeps such a result off `main`, so it stays on local disk and out of the
# repository. Recover it again by FULL IMMUTABLE SHA (rule 33 [R-SHARD-ARCHIVE]
# (d)), never by branch name:
#   git archive bb3034214d1d3da70d0db8d8435540f82387222d results/calibration/caiso287_instr_2022 | tar -x -C .
# (`git archive | tar -x` rather than `git checkout <sha> -- <path>`, which
# STAGES what it writes and can silently revert whatever landed on main since.)
results/calibration/caiso287_instr_2022/

